reasons":{"not SLP1-clean":10054,"Devanagari render is lossy (unresolved sandhi)":11049}},"provenance":{"vaidika_padas_total":463281,"vaidika_needs_review":8060,"vaidika_punarukti":8752,"yaugika_dhatus":40,"yaugika_dhatus_available":2229,"yaugika_vedic_forms":379,"vidyut_commit":"8da2f90bee3ce1c07505fa432fc3729e3f7e02ea","print_convention":"rigvedic","krdanta_sweep_stems":862849,"krdanta_sweep_forms":1708513},"known_limits":["Vaidika loci are structurally valid but NOT citable: L1–L3 codes are placeholders until the VedaNidhi vākya code table is supplied. The manual calls this the single hardest blocker to Phase 0.","Vaidika entries are inflected padapāṭha forms, not lemmas. `pada` carries no lemma link yet, so a Veda word cannot be joined to its kośa attestation automatically — the join shown here is by identical surface form only.","Yaugika stems are DERIVED, and most are textually silent: the kṛt sweep produces them from the Dhātupāṭha whether or not any author ever used them. A stem marked 'in no kośa' is well-formed Sanskrit, not attested Sanskrit.","The stem sweep is kṛt only — dhātu × kṛt pratyaya × upasarga. Taddhitānta, samāsa and uṇādi derivations are not swept, so this is the kṛdanta prātipadika space, not the whole yaugika space.","The inflected-form layer, the only place the sūtra chain itself is shown, is still a 40-dhātu sample of 2,229.","No source is excluded. Sources in copyright, sources whose licence is unestablished, English-keyed dictionaries and proper-name catalogues are all searchable — which means some hits are English words or personal names rather than Sanskrit vocabulary. Each card names its source so a reader can judge.","The four-school stem analysis of manual §5 ships School A only. Schools B (Nirukta), C (Sthaulāṣṭhīvi) and D (Śākapūṇi) have no data behind them yet.","Manual §6 grammarian philosophy, §7 vivakṣā flags and §9 coinage engine are not built. They are shown as planned, never as empty features.","A render gate withholds keys that are not SLP1-clean (a locus or catalogue numeral that leaked into a headword) and keys whose Devanagari cannot be written without loss — hyphen-compound padapāṭha rows whose sandhi was never resolved. They are counted on the Corpus tab, not silently dropped."]}